From 0781a8338faf48e3a019ca3bbfffeac6abe55b91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:02:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: draw GL through the TA/3D path

pvr_draw.c moves the probe's verified render path into the driver:
draws accumulate into one control stream per render target and the
render (geometry + fragment) is submitted at flush, readback or target
change. Each draw gets a TA state block from the GL state (viewport,
region clip), a vertex PDS program built from the bound vertex elements
and buffers, and the bound VS/FS. The FS is compiled per colour-buffer
format; a colour clear becomes the render's background object; the
end-of-tile program, the scissor table and the HWRT data set (sized
from the framebuffer with pvr_hwrt_sizes) are built here. Anything the
path does not handle yet falls back to the compute rasteriser.

Fixes found on the way (a real GL draw exercises them, the probe did
not):
- the index-list packet never set index_base_addrmsb, so an index
  buffer above 4 GiB was read from the wrong address;
- the heap carveouts with the firmware's static programs were mapped
  only by the probe (pvr_static_memory_init), so the TA read unmapped
  memory;
- fragment shaders were compiled with fs.z_replicate = 0, which makes
  pco write the fragment depth over colour output 0, and without
  no_alpha_to_coverage/skip_sample_check, which insert a coverage test
  that reads a shared register nothing fills and discards every
  fragment;
- gl_FragColor (FRAG_RESULT_COLOR) now maps to DATA0 with the output
  format and range set, as the Vulkan driver does;
- the colour clear mask check compared the whole 32-bit mask to 0xf.

The context also gets the hooks a GL draw needs: vertex elements and
sampler state objects, sampler views, buffer/texture subdata, scissor/
blend colour/clip/stipple, copy, a CPU blit for same-format copies,
clears and barriers.

A GLES2 program (EGL surfaceless, FBO, glClear + glDrawArrays with its
own shaders) now renders the same image through the native driver as
through zink: 32768 red pixels on green, Kick TA -> TA finished ->
Kick 3D -> 3D finished. Not yet: varyings, uniforms, textures, depth,
blending, culling, loading a target without a clear.
